  m_text: When sunlight falls on the plant, it is absorbed by chlorophyll present
    in the leaves. This light energy starts the process of photosynthesis by converting
    solar energy into chemical energy in the form of ATP and NADPH. During this stage,
    water molecules are split, preparing energy for food production.
